# ApexYard

> ApexYard gives your agents a team's process, then checks every pull request against it. The framework is open source (MIT).

## Your agents write the code. Your process decides what merges.

ApexYard gives your agents a team's process, then checks every pull request against it.

Agent agnostic. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and OpenCode.

## One process, three places

Keel is your team's rules and context, read by every agent. Developers write a rule once. Build, the Gate and Readiness all work from it. A miss comes back as a new rule.

1. **Developers** (write and approve rules): A developer writes the rule. A second developer approves it.
2. **Keel** (your team's rules and context): Every change starts from a ticket.
3. **Build** (agents read Keel while they write): The agent reads the rule over MCP. It opens a ticket before it writes code.
4. **Gate** (checks each pull request against Keel): A pull request with no ticket cannot merge.
5. **Readiness** (measures each repository against Keel): It flags repositories where changes skip tickets.
6. **A miss** (becomes a new rule in Keel): A review finds a ticket with no test plan. The fix becomes a new rule in Keel.

- About Build: <https://apexyard.ai/build>
- About Gate: <https://apexyard.ai/gate>
- About Readiness: <https://apexyard.ai/readiness>

Underneath: Keel, one evidence store and one dashboard.

It never reads your code. See what the GitHub App can see: <https://apexyard.ai/gate#app-access>.

## Install Build for free

Give your agents tickets, plans and reviewers today. Every rule, hook and review agent is a plain file you can read, change or remove.

Fork <https://github.com/me2resh/apexyard> into your organisation on GitHub. Then run these commands.

```sh
# macOS
brew install jq
git clone https://github.com/your-org/apexyard.git
cd apexyard
bash bin/apexyard doctor

# Linux
sudo apt-get install jq
git clone https://github.com/your-org/apexyard.git
cd apexyard
bash bin/apexyard doctor
```

On Fedora, use `sudo dnf install jq`.

On Windows, use Git Bash (from Git for Windows) or WSL. The hooks are Bash scripts. PowerShell and cmd.exe cannot run them. In Git Bash, install jq with `winget install jqlang.jq`. Then run the clone, cd and doctor commands above. In WSL, use the Linux commands.

Then open Claude Code in the folder and run `/setup`. Read the install guide for Codex, Cursor and OpenCode: <https://apexyard.ai/docs/quickstart/install>.

